    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor with an elite efficiency score of 83.29. He faces Hunter Brown in a matchup where his 14% platoon edge and favorable spot in the order combine to maximize his production ceiling. Meanwhile, our speed-focused strategy is bolstered by **Nasim Nunez** (70.00) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (66.92), both of whom benefit significantly from facing the soft-tossing Jacob Lopez. These plays are prioritized to keep our stolen base volume competitive; their elevated scores are driven largely by their SP skill advantage and the high-scoring potential of their respective matchups. **Sam Antonacci** (63.13) and **Miguel Vargas** (62.63) also represent strong starts, with each benefiting from the 19% SP skill boost provided by Trey Yesavage\u2019s favorable xERA projection.\n\nWe have opted to bench **Curtis Mead** (60.33) despite his respectable efficiency, as the depth of our middle infield\u2014anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jacob Wilson**\u2014pushed him to the outside of the starting nine. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.82) also narrowly missed the cut; while his talent is undeniable, the tough matchup against Sean Burke diluted his daily floor compared to the more favorable platoon situations exploited by our current starters. We are closely monitoring the 45% rain risk surrounding **Jackson Merrill** (54.33); if the weather worsens, we may need to rotate in a bench bat to avoid a zero, though his current score remains high enough to warrant the risk for now. **Cole Carrigg** faces a challenging hurdle against Hunter Greene, whose elite stuff mandates caution, but his park factor at least provides a marginal buffer to his efficiency projection.",
